WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.320
Norway went electric faster than any country on Earth. Its old gasoline cars just changed

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:12.380
address. This is Unintended Consequences, episode 97. In a warehouse lot outside Dramen,

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:19.560
a 2014 Volkswagen Passat sits with its Norwegian plates already unscrewed. The winter tires are still

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:25.860
in the trunk. The service book is complete. Within a month, that same car will be on a lot in Vilnius

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:33.320
or Poznan, advertised as a one-owner Nordic import, well-maintained, rust-free, ready for another decade

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:39.040
of commuting. The policy that put it there was built to take gasoline cars off Norwegian roads.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.900
It moved them onto someone else's. Norway did not stumble into electric cars. It built the world's

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:51.960
most generous demand-side electric vehicle regime on purpose. Over three decades, for reasons that

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:58.880
were internally consistent. Electricity in Norway is almost entirely hydropower. By the 1990s,

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.740
the grid was already among the cleanest on Earth. What was not clean was the tailpipe.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.700
Transport was one of the largest remaining sources of domestic greenhouse gas emissions.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.480
In a country that sold North Sea oil to the world, had both the money and the political need to

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:20.600
decarbonize what happened on its own roads. The starting began stacking privileges in 1990,

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:26.600
with an exemption from registration tax. Free municipal parking and a cut in the annual tax

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:34.740
followed in 1996. toll roads opened without charge in 1997. The decisive blow came in 2001.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:41.220
Electric cars were exempted from the 25% value-added tax that every other new vehicle paid.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:46.860
Later came bust lane access, reduced ferry fares, and company car tax advantages.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.140
None of this was a Lark. Norway already taxed internal combustion cars heavily.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:59.020
By weight, by carbon dioxide, by nitrogen oxides. So the same fiscal machinery that made a gasoline

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:05.320
sport utility vehicle expensive could make an electric one look cheap. Across labor and conservative

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:11.460
governments the coalition held. Because the policy served several audiences at once. Climate targets,

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.760
a visible answer to the charge that an oil state was a climate hypocrite. And a high income

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:23.700
public that liked new cars. In 2017 the storting wrote the ambition into the national transport plan.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:31.160
All new passenger cars and light vans should be zero emission by 2025. Given the information on the

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:36.940
table, a clean grid, a tax system already built for steering, and a sovereign wealth cushion,

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:43.560
the design was rational. Those stacked exemptions did not stay on paper. They compounded at the

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:49.070
ownership. The incentives were not a single program so much as a pile of exemptions that stacked

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:55.170
on top of one another. On a mid-range electric car, the value-added tax holiday alone was worth

00:02:55.170 --> 00:03:00.970
tens of thousands of Corona. Add the waived purchase tax, and the electric vehicle often undercut

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:07.490
a comparable gasoline model after tax. Charging networks thickened along the E6 and in the cities.

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:14.290
The Norwegian EV Association, Elbil for Ainingen, became one of the most effective consumer lobbies

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:19.390
in the country, translating each new registration record into an argument for keeping the perks.

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:26.050
Early numbers looked like a case study in policy that works. Electric cars and plug-in hybrids were a

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:37.470
curiosity in the 2000s. By 2019 they were more than 40% of new passenger car sales. In 2020 the share

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:45.950
it approached 4 in 5. By 2023 and 2024, depending on the month, 9 of 10 new cars leaving Norwegian

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:52.810
dealerships had a plug. Oslo's air monitors recorded fewer nitrogen oxide spikes. National

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:58.670
inventory reports showed transport emissions bending down. Proponents, including ministers under

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:05.210
Air and a Solberg and later Jonas Garsterra, could point to a real domestic result. The new car fleet

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:11.290
had been transformed faster than in any other large market. Skeptics existed, but they mostly argued

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:18.030
about cost. The tax expenditure per car. The crowding of bus lanes. The fairness of subsidizing

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:24.110
Tesla's for affluent households in Baram. What the Skeptics did not organize around, at least not

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:30.150
at first, was the secondary market. Almost no one in the original design debate treated the used

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:36.510
gasoline car as a policy object. The car that left the Norwegian fleet was assumed implicitly

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:43.150
to have left the problem. A new car miracle is also a used car flood. Norwegian households

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:49.710
did not add an electric vehicle on top of the old Volvo. They replaced it. Domestic demand for used

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:55.690
gasoline and diesel cars softened just as supply jumped. Because the same incentives that made a new

00:04:55.690 --> 00:05:01.150
ID4 or Model Y irresistible made a seven-year-old Passat harder to sell at home.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:07.550
Exporters stepped into the gap. Norway already had the apparatus of a rich country used vehicle

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:13.550
trade. Strict periodic inspections, complete service histories, a climate that is hard on salt

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:20.390
but easy on rust compared with wetter poor markets. Eastern Europe already had the demand. Lithuania

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:26.630
in particular had become a continental clearinghouse for used cars. Poland, Bulgaria, Romania,

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:32.110
and the Baltic states were ready buyers. Tens of thousands of used passenger cars left more

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:37.570
way in the peak years of the transition. A rising share of them, the gasoline and diesel vehicles that

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:43.390
the electric boom had orphaned. Those cars did not go to scrap yards. They went onto fairies and

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:49.730
into sealed trucks and they went back into traffic. The mechanism is what researchers later described as

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:55.250
accelerated vintage transfer across regulatory borders. Every country retires cars.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.830
Wealthy countries normally export a large fraction of what they deregister rather than crush it.

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:07.310
Norway's incentives did not invent that trade. They sped it up and skewed its contents. People

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:12.970
replaced usable internal combustion cars earlier than they otherwise would have, which meant the vehicles

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:18.470
crossing the border were not end of life wrecks. They were midlife cars with years of service left

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:24.410
and they were, on average, dirtier than the fleet they were leaving. Fleet data showed that the

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:29.790
exported vehicles carried higher average tailpipe emissions than the Norwegian passenger car average

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:36.010
before the policy had done its work. That is the opposite of a clean retirement. It is a spatial

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:42.050
reshuffle of the high emitting tail of the fleet. Second order effects followed the cars. In the

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:47.690
destination countries, a well kept Norwegian diesel is not a curiosity. It is a bargain with a

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:53.210
reputation. A Norwegian diesel competes with new cars, including the first cheap electrics,

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:59.070
and it competes with whatever older local vehicle it displaces. If that diesel replaces a

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:05.510
still dirtier 2000s car, local air quality can improve. If it simply adds cheap mobility,

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:10.790
or if it postpones the moment when a Polish or Lithuanian household would have faced a new car

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:16.410
market already tilting electric, it extends the life of internal combustion under another flag.

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:23.270
Either way, the kilometers do not vanish. They migrate. Some of the same vehicles are re-exported

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:30.070
again from Vilnius toward the Caucasus, Central Asia, or West Africa. A third order hop that lengthens

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:35.390
the chain and moves the emissions into places with weaker inspection regimes and longer remaining

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:41.050
vehicle life. Embodied carbon in the steel and aluminum stays in service, which is not nothing,

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:45.810
but the tailpipe carbon that Norway no longer counts keeps accumulating somewhere

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:52.490
the Norwegian inventory does not see. Accounting made the irony durable. Under the territorial rules of

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:58.170
the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change, a ton of carbon dioxide emitted on a ring

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:04.630
road outside Kraków does not appear in Oslo's ledger. Norway could report a cleaner national fleet,

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:11.410
a collapsing new sales emissions average, and visible progress toward the 2025 zero emission target,

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:17.690
all of which were true inside the border. The net European reduction was smaller than those domestic

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:23.770
figures suggested, because the policy had not destroyed a stock of gasoline cars. It had changed

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:29.350
their address and, by pulling replacement forward, had quite possibly increased the number of years

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:35.430
those particular engines would run. The cars that left were worse than the cars that stayed. The success

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:40.850
metric never asked where they went. There is a human texture to this that is easy to miss if the

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:46.970
story is told only as a chart. A family in Bergen trades a diesel station wagon for a used Tesla

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:53.790
and feels, correctly, that they have done the thing the state asked. A dealer in Kownes puts Norska

00:08:53.790 --> 00:09:00.830
Bealer on the windscreen because Norwegian origin is a quality signal, one owner, full books, inspection

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:07.290
passed. A nurse in Wudj buys that car because a safe heated affordable car is not an abstraction.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:14.170
Nobody in that chain is cheating. The incentive did exactly what incentives do. It reallocated

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:19.810
objects toward the people who now valued the most. The object in question happened to be a source of

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:26.150
carbon dioxide, and the valuation happened to flip at a national border. Norway did not reverse the

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:31.190
electric vehicle project, and it should not be pretended that the project failed on its own terms.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:37.130
New car electrification is close to complete. What changed is the generosity at the margin,

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:44.790
and, more slowly, the conversation about system boundaries. From 2023, value added tax was applied

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:51.310
to the portion of an electric vehicle's price above 500,000 Kroner. Weight-based taxes began to claw

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:56.950
back some of the advantage of the heaviest electric sport utility vehicles. Bus lane privileges and

00:09:57.010 --> 00:10:02.070
toll discounts had already been tightened in Oslo and other cities after congestion and political

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:08.810
backlash. These were fiscal and urban corrections, not a reckoning with exports. The used internal

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:14.530
combustion outflow continues because the underlying arithmetic continues. Norwegian households

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:20.330
still prefer to sell than to scrap, and Eastern European households still prefer a cheap, solid

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:25.990
combustion car to a new electric they cannot finance. When the leakage became harder to ignore,

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:32.330
in research institutes, in the European used vehicle literature, in the fine print of fleet statistics,

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:37.870
the obvious fix presented itself. Pair the purchase subsidy with a scrapage requirement,

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:44.090
so the old car dies instead of emigrating. That fix carries its own unintended consequence.

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:51.130
Croshing a working 2015 Passat wastes the carbon already spent to manufacture it, and it does not

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:56.270
guarantee a cleaner outcome downstream. The household in Vilnius will still need a car.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:11:01.410
If the Norwegian one is gone, the next cheapest import may be older or dirtier,

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:05.550
or drawn from another Western European market that is running the same play.

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:12.410
Germany's used car exports into Poland and beyond are a parallel river. Mandatory scrapage can

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:18.190
satisfy a territorial inventory and still fail a European one, while adding a pile of shredded

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:24.110
metal that had years of use left. The European Union has edged toward tighter roadworthiness and

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:30.450
end-of-life vehicle rules for exports, and researchers have begun to treat used vehicle trade as a first-class

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:37.210
climate variable rather than a footnote. Norway, for now, remains the showcase. The showcase still

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:43.970
does not count the cars that left. Three principles travel beyond Oslo. First, the perimeter of measurement

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:49.870
is a policy choice, not a natural fact. If you score a program inside a border, you will harvest

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:54.970
transfers and call them reductions. Incentive structures will find the edge of the scoreboard.

00:11:55.530 --> 00:12:01.550
Second, accelerating turnover is not the same as retiring a technology. The fate of the displaced

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:07.930
stock, scrap, export, second-life, third-life is where a large share of the physical consequence

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:14.190
actually happens, and secondary markets are not around any error. Third, the repair can be as

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:19.990
leaky as the original design. Scrapage satisfies the inventory and can waste immobodied carbon.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:26.370
Doing nothing satisfies the used car buyer and can lengthen the tailpipe's life. Neither is free.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:32.690
The forward question is already live. As Germany, France, the United Kingdom, and the United States

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:37.390
push electric vehicle adoption up the same steep curve Norway has already climbed,

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:43.130
their gasoline and diesel fleets will have to go somewhere. Some will go to Mexico, some to

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:48.810
Eastern Europe, some to West Africa. The mechanism does not require fjords or hydropower.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:54.330
It requires a subsidy on one side of a border and a functioning resale market on the other.

00:12:54.950 --> 00:13:00.030
The only open issue is whether the next country to declare victory will bother to follow the cars.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:05.530
And that's where today's story leaves us. If it changed how you see one every day decision,

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:11.170
that's the whole point. Pass it along to someone who depreciated, and we'll be back tomorrow with

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:16.430
another case. And if you'd rather watch, then listen, find us on YouTube at Narra Network,

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:21.970
links in the show notes. Quick tip from the network, try the do-positive pod next.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:28.310
Good news and science and tech, plus one concrete action you can take. Every Narra Network show is

